        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7116478b-9110-5a8c-8cdf-5801b7d51db5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kyosuke Himuro, Boy George, Yukinojo Mori, Dominic J. Hawken, George Alan O'Dowd, Takuro Yoshida, Junichi Inagaki, Marilyn\n- Organizations: Boøwy\n- Works: \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\", \"Karma Chameleon\", \"Dragon Ball Z\"\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, musician, lead vocalist, DJ, fashion designer, photographer, keyboard player, session musician, songwriter\n- Places: Takasaki, Gunma, Japan\n\nFacts:\n- Kyosuke Himuro was born on October 7, 1960, in Takasaki, Gunma, Japan.\n- Boy George, born George Alan O'Dowd, was born on 14 June 1961 and is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer, and photographer.\n- Dominic J. Hawken was born in 1967.\n- Kyosuke Himuro is a Japanese singer-songwriter and musician.\n- Kyosuke Himuro was the lead vocalist of the rock band Boøwy from 1981 to 1988.\n- During the 1980s, Boy George's band recorded global hit songs including \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me,\" \"Time (Clock of the Heart),\" and \"Karma Chameleon.\"\n- Boy George is known for his soulful voice and androgynous appearance.\n- Dominic J. Hawken was a keyboard player and session musician in the 1990s and originally played with Boy George and Marilyn.\n- Yukinojo Mori has written over 2,000 songs for artists including Kyosuke Himuro, Takuro Yoshida, and Junichi Inagaki.\n- Yukinojo Mori also wrote theme songs for anime series including \"Dragon Ball Z\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "db9ed8e6-7429-5d22-80e7-c47820a929a3",
        "text": "Page: Kyosuke Himuro. Sentence: Kyosuke Himuro (氷室 京介 , Himuro Kyōsuke , born October 7, 1960 in Takasaki, Gunma, Japan) is a Japanese singer-songwriter and musician.\nPage: Kyosuke Himuro. Sentence: He was a lead vocalist of the rock band Boøwy from 1981 to 1988.\nPage: Boy George. Sentence: Boy George (born George Alan O'Dowd; 14 June 1961) is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer and photographer.\nPage: Boy George. Sentence: At the height of the band's fame, during the 1980s, they recorded global hit songs such as \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\" and \"Karma Chameleon\" and George is known for his soulful voice and androgynous appearance.\nPage: Yukinojo Mori. Sentence: He has written over 2,000 songs for numerous artists such as Kyosuke Himuro, Takuro Yoshida and Junichi Inagaki and theme songs for anime series including \"Dragon Ball Z\".\nPage: Dominic Hawken. Sentence: Dominic J. Hawken (born 1967) was a keyboard player and session musician in the 1990s, originally playing with Boy George and Marilyn.",
